<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >Once explained/elaborated, you do make so much more sense Shadis. <img src="images/smilies/smile.gif" border=0> I would love to see future RPGs defintely be, you know, ROLEPLAYING oriented. It looks like it might head that way with some of the 2nd Generation games (NWN comes to mind with the human GM at the wheel), but not all of them. I consider DAoC like EQ 1.5...it looks great, prolly wont be as easy to RP as I want, wont have the VI/Sony bullshit problems, etc, etc. Thats what I am hoping at least. But I dont expect it to be really deepy roleplaying...and I am ok with that.<br>
<br>
There are defintely 'fantasy action games' out there now. True roleplaying can happen in them, but the games arent centered around it. But maybe someone will develop one or a system or whatever. The genre is young and all those excuses. <img src="images/smilies/wink.gif" border=0> One reason I dig White Wolfs World Of Darkness line is the RP aspect. The #'s are there, but they arent the focus. Well, they could be, but not by any Storyteller that expects me to stick the fuck around.<br>
<br>
Kith the Half-PowerGamer Half-Roleplayer (though Min'd probably tell ya it was 90/10...heh)</font></p>

